  "result": "I've written the rule and its 15 witnesses for LVMC_11_16_040, and the gate returned **OK**. I used 3 of the 6 runs, and the first was wasted because I ran it on the skeleton before writing anything.\n\n**How the rule reads:**\n- **Who and when:** the subject is a vehicle that occupies an intersection j. The conditions are checked once, at the moment it enters j, and carry over for as long as it stays in j.\n- **Restricted view (d4, d6–d8):** at some point in the last 100 ft of the subject's path before entering j, one of these held:\n  - the intersection's sight distance was shorter than the subject's distance to it;\n  - sight along a road meeting at j was under 100 ft;\n  - another road user on such a road, within 100 ft of j, was not visible to the subject.\n- **Through-street exception (d9):** checked at the last observation before entry. The subject's approach lane has no stop sign, yield sign or flashing-red signal, and another lane entering j has one. If the subject is in several lanes entering j, none of them may be controlled, so the rule never picks the lane that favours the subject.\n- **Traffic-controlled exception (d10):** while the subject is in j, a signal that isn't dark, a stop sign or a yield sign governs j or a lane entering it.\n- **Duty (d1):** speed at most 15 mph while in j.\n\n**Choices the node left open:**\n- **The subject isn't part of the traffic it has to see.** Otherwise the rule would need a \"visible to itself\" value, which no source records.\n- **\"The observation before entry\" for d9** is found within the same 100 ft path window. If the subject's observations are more than 100 ft apart, the exception doesn't apply.\n- **d10 is checked at each moment the subject is in j,** because the record gives no time.\n- **No narrowings declared.**\n\n**Node issue for the plan (not a blocker):** d9 is almost entirely covered by d10. Any stop sign, yield sign or flashing-red signal on a lane entering j already makes j traffic-controlled, so with signs and signals that don't change, d9 can never change a verdict. The gate also rejects devices that appear in only some scenes. The only witnesses that exercise d9 use a signal that shows flashing red during the approach and goes dark when the subject enters (branch_9 and branch_15). The plan may want to reconsider whether d9 should stay a separate exception.\n\nFiles are in `library/` under the worktree:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_16_040.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_16_040.lean`\n- `task_result.md`, in the working directory",
